readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	ooo_readme.GettingInvolved.emptyparagraph.A5	a			0	sa-IN	The best way to start contributing is to subscribe to one or more of the mailing lists, lurk for a while, and gradually use the mail archives to familiarize yourself with many of the topics covered since the ${PRODUCTNAME} source code was released back in October 2000. When you're comfortable, all you need to do is send an email self-introduction and jump right in. If you are familiar with Open Source Projects, check out our To-Dos list and see if there is anything you would like to help with at 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
